[1] [4] To make a particular user account usable only by WebSocket clients, you would restrict the allowed connection types for that user to include only WebSocket clients. In the configuration, for a user named `bar` that would be set up as follows:

```plaintext
authorization {
  users [ 
    { 
      user: bar, 
      password: barpwd, 
      permission: {...}, 
      allowed_connection_types: ["WEBSOCKET"] 
    } 
  ]
}
```

This configuration ensures that only connections via WebSocket are accepted for that user account.

[1] To make a particular user account usable only by WebSocket clients and not regular NATS connections, the user's connection types must be restricted to WebSocket. This can be achieved by adding the `allowed_connection_types` option to the user's configuration and specifying `"WEBSOCKET"` as the value. The updated user configuration would look like this:

```text
authorization {
  users [
    {user: foo password: foopwd, permission: {...}}
    {user: bar password: barpwd, permission: {...}, allowed_connection_types: ["WEBSOCKET"]}
  ]
}
```
